      "has_diagram": false,
      "has_bullets": false,
      "extraction_quality": "good",
      "source_extraction": "pdftotext",
      "technical_purpose": "Spindle failed to orient",
      "text": "116 Spindle Orientation Fault\nSpindle did not orient correctly. This is either a vector drive\nproblem or a mechanical problem on machines without a vector\ndrive. During a spindle orientation function, the spindle is\nrotated until the lock pin drops in; but the lock pin never dropped.\nParameters 66, 70, 73, and 74 can adjust delays and spindle\norient speeds. This can be caused by a trip of circuit breaker\nCB4, a lack of air pressure, or too much friction with the\norientation pin.",
      "revision_group": "vf_alarm_116",
      "is_revision_pair": true
    },
