      "pdf_page_start_1based": 57,
      "pdf_page_end_1based": 57,
      "source_role": "revision_reference",
      "revision_priority": 2,
      "has_table": false,
      "has_diagram": false,
      "has_bullets": false,
      "extraction_quality": "good",
      "source_extraction": "pdftotext",
      "technical_purpose": "Tool shuttle failed to move fully IN",
      "text": "113 Shuttle In Fault\nTool changer is not completely to right. During a tool changer\noperation the tool in/out shuttle failed to get to the IN position.\nParameters 62 and 63 can adjust the time-out times. This alarm\ncan be caused by anything that jams the motion of the slide or by\nthe presence of a tool in the pocket facing the spindle. A loss of\npower to the tool changer can also cause this. Check relays K9K12, and fuse F1 on IOPCB.",
      "revision_group": "vf_alarm_113",
      "is_revision_pair": true
    },
