      "alarm_text": "Turret Rotate Fault",
      "subsystem": "tool changer",
      "manual_page_start": 57,
      "manual_page_end": 57,
      "pdf_page_start_1based": 57,
      "pdf_page_end_1based": 57,
      "source_role": "revision_reference",
      "revision_priority": 2,
      "has_table": false,
      "has_diagram": false,
      "has_bullets": false,
      "extraction_quality": "good",
      "source_extraction": "pdftotext",
      "technical_purpose": "Turret/carousel rotation fault",
      "text": "115 Turret Rotate Fault\nTool carousel motor not in position. During a tool changer\noperation the tool turret failed to start moving, failed to stop\nmoving or failed to stop at the right position. Parameters 60 and\n61 can adjust the time-out times. This alarm can be caused by\nanything that jams the rotation of the turret. A loss of power to the\ntool changer can also cause this. Check relays K9-K12, and fuse\nF1 on IOPCB.",
      "revision_group": "vf_alarm_115",
      "is_revision_pair": true
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "vf_2001_revc_alarm_116",
