      "chunk_type": "alarm",
      "alarm_number": 122,
      "alarm_text": "Regen Overheat",
      "subsystem": "electrical/spindle",
      "manual_page_start": 58,
      "manual_page_end": 58,
      "pdf_page_start_1based": 58,
      "pdf_page_end_1based": 58,
      "source_role": "revision_reference",
      "revision_priority": 2,
      "has_table": false,
      "has_diagram": false,
      "has_bullets": false,
      "extraction_quality": "good",
      "source_extraction": "pdftotext",
      "technical_purpose": "Regenerative load/control overheating",
      "text": "122 Regen Overheat\nThe regenerative load temperature is above a safe limit. This\nalarm will turn off the spindle drive, coolant pump, and tool\nchanger. One common cause of this overheat condition is an\ninput line voltage too high. If this condition persists, an automatic\nshutdown will begin after the interval specified by parameter 297.\nIt can also be caused by a high start/stop duty cycle of spindle.",
      "revision_group": "vf_alarm_122",
      "is_revision_pair": true
    },
